cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "TSL: Time Series Logging"
type: software
abstract: >-
  TSL (Time Series Logging) is a library for cyclically logging a large number of time
  series signals from C++ and Python with very low overhead (~69 ns per signal). It
  targets real-time robotics software, where frequently changing internal debug signals
  would otherwise break the compatibility of previously recorded rosbags on every ROS 2
  message definition change. The logger is separated from the publisher, so
  instrumenting a module introduces no ROS 2 dependency and parsing the published
  ROS 2 messages is supported by PlotJuggler.
